Ldap.Answer.description:
What the directory said. `ok` is false for every result code but success
(and, for a compare, compareTrue and compareFalse, which are both answers);
`stoppedAt: "bind"` says the bind was refused and nothing followed it.

Tls.Handshake.description:
One handshake. `connected` says whether the TLS session was established;
`usable` whether it was still good once the peer had had its say — a TLS
1.3 server refuses a client certificate AFTER the handshake completes.
